1:0-66 "/// The four other Lua rules of Resource/Schema/rules/, rewritten." comment.line.documentation.canon
2:0-3 "///" comment.line.documentation.canon
3:0-83 "/// Each record below is trimmed to the fields its rule reads; the real types would" comment.line.documentation.canon
4:0-85 "/// carry every field of their file, be public and documented. Here they are `local`:" comment.line.documentation.canon
5:0-87 "/// the point is the rules. In Canon they are ordinary `check`s, next to the data, with" comment.line.documentation.canon
6:0-86 "/// no keyword vocabulary to argue about (\"a keyword with one user, clause 2 refuses\")" comment.line.documentation.canon
7:0-23 "/// and no type guards." comment.line.documentation.canon
8:0-3 "///" comment.line.documentation.canon
9:0-83 "/// Since ADR-0009 (resourcestudio, 2026-09-19) the Lua files are these rules' only" comment.line.documentation.canon
10:0-87 "/// implementation: Resource Studio's Go copies (internal/rules/) were deleted, and the" comment.line.documentation.canon
11:0-89 "/// studio asks validate.py. Here the rules also run on the files themselves: each record" comment.line.documentation.canon
12:0-67 "/// is loaded below, so `canon check` reports what the Lua reports." comment.line.documentation.canon
